{"ticker":"BX","updated":"2026-10-30T22:37:56Z","profile":{"longName":"Blackstone Inc.","shortName":"Blackstone Inc.","sector":"Financial Services","industry":"Asset Management","country":"United States","website":"https://www.blackstone.com","fullTimeEmployees":5285,"marketCap":141654736896,"trailingPE":26.39421,"forwardPE":16.06164,"priceToSalesTrailing12Months":9.157999,"pegRatio":1.19,"targetMeanPrice":138.86365,"targetHighPrice":169.0,"targetLowPrice":118.0,"numberOfAnalystOpinions":22,"recommendationKey":"buy","revenueGrowth":-0.005,"earningsGrowth":0.037,"grossMargins":1.0,"operatingMargins":0.48860002,"profitMargins":0.22993,"totalRevenue":15467870208,"beta":1.587,"fiftyTwoWeekHigh":165.14,"fiftyTwoWeekLow":101.73,"currency":"USD","exchange":"NYQ","quoteType":"EQUITY","dividendYield":4.34},"summary":"Blackstone Inc. is an alternative asset management firm specializing in private equity, venture capital, real estate, hedge fund solutions, credit, secondary funds of funds, public debt and equity and multi-asset class strategies. The firm typically invests in early-stage, seed, middle market, mature, late venture, growth capital, emerging growth, turnaround, and later stage companies. It also provide capital markets services. The real estate segment specializes in opportunistic, core+ investments as well as debt investment opportunities collateralized by commercial real estate, and stabilized income-oriented commercial real estate across North America, Europe and Asia. Within fund of fund investments, it seeks to invest in private equity funds, venture capital funds, mezzanine funds, distressed debt/turnaround funds, secondary investment funds & real estate funds. The firm's corporate private equity business pursues transactions throughout the world across a variety of transaction types, including large buyouts, recapitalization, special situations, distressed mortgage loans, mid-cap buyouts, buy and build platforms, which involves multiple acquisitions behind 